# Schedule

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Desk.Models`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Desk.Core`

## Purpose
Pure-data model of when a scheduled agent should fire, plus a `Next(from)`
computation that produces the next fire time for any given reference time, and
a `ScheduleBuilder` for fluent construction.

## Definition

```csharp
public class Schedule
{
    public ScheduleInterval Interval { get; set; } = ScheduleInterval.None;
    public ScheduleAtTime? AtTime { get; set; }
    public ScheduleAtEvery? AtEvery { get; set; }
    public ScheduleWeekly? Weekly { get; set; }
    public ScheduleMonthly? Monthly { get; set; }

    public void Validate();
    public DateTime? Next(DateTime from);

    public enum ScheduleInterval { None, Minute, Hourly, Daily, Weekly, Monthly, Custom }
    public class ScheduleAtTime { /* Hour, Minute, Second, validated [0,23][0,59][0,59] */ }
    public class ScheduleAtEvery { /* Hour, Minute, Second, all >= 0, not all zero */ }
    public class ScheduleWeekly { /* Day, Time */ }
    public class ScheduleMonthly { /* Day 1..31, Time */ }
}

public class ScheduleBuilder
{
    public ScheduleBuilder WithInterval(Schedule.ScheduleInterval interval);
    public ScheduleBuilder AtTime(int hour, int minute, int second);
    public ScheduleBuilder ExecuteEvery(int hour, int minute, int second);
    public ScheduleBuilder On(DayOfWeek day, int hour, int minute, int second);
    public ScheduleBuilder OnDayOfMonth(int day, int hour, int minute, int second);
    public Schedule Build();
}
```

## Validate
Throws `InvalidOperationException` if a required payload is missing for the
selected interval. Safe to call after manual construction; `Build()` calls it
automatically.

## Next(from)
Computes the next fire time strictly after `from`, based on `Interval` and the
matching payload. Returns `DateTime.UtcNow`-style values.

- `None` → `null` (scheduler deletes the agent and logs)
- `Minute` → `from.AddMinutes(1)`
- `Hourly` → `from.AddHours(1)`
- `Daily` → next occurrence of `AtTime` on or after `from`, advancing one day if `from` is already past today's slot
- `Weekly` → next occurrence of `Weekly.Day` at `Weekly.Time` on or after `from`, advancing one week if `from` is already past this week's slot
- `Monthly` → next occurrence of `Monthly.Day` at `Monthly.Time` in `from`'s month (clamped to last day for short months like Feb 31), advancing to next month if `from` is already past this month's slot
- `Custom` → next slot of `AtEvery` period strictly after `from`

Throws `InvalidOperationException` if a required payload is missing, or if
`Custom` period is zero.

## ScheduleBuilder
Fluent builder. Each setter clears all payloads first, then sets the matching
one. `Build()` calls `Validate()` and returns the constructed `Schedule`.
